                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "28/10/2026\n\nvalve deadass just packaged quake with a texture pack and called it \"Deathmatch Classic\" anyway buy the game because its quake\n\nwait why is \"Day of Defeat\" in the \"Counter-Strike Anthology\" bundle, valve be tripping for real\n\nlol the recommended linux version is ubuntu 12.04, that literally came out in 2012\n\nwhy is the recommended ram 128mb, quake recommended 16mb when that came out\n\ni wonder if this version of VAC is just as good at stopping cheaters as the current version used in counter strike nowadays\n\nthe portals literally swirl around in the same pattern as the ones in quake just with a more weird looking texture, its pretty funny seeing gman running around with a thunderbolt actually along with the nailguns that are trying to hard to be real guns\n\nso like im meant to be revising chemistry and physics right now since they are difficult and i did shit on the last tests but im enjoying writing this review since i know nobodys gonna see it for years, do you understand the lyman spectrum? i certainly struggle with it but im not entirely sure its impossible. the thing i find most difficult is the calculations and the electron structure. did you know that sodium is written as \"[Ne] 3s1\" with the \"[Ne]\" being a neon core so you dont have to write out the full thing?\n\ni might come back and update this review another time",
